node_modules/
.env
# THE OPERATIONAL RECORD IS EVIDENCE TOO, AND UNTIL NOW THE RULE THREW IT AWAY.
#
# out/ holds the turn-by-turn run logs, the ladder's own log, each directive
# watcher's delivery record and the held-out verifier's JSON results. logs/ holds
# the operator-side transcripts. None of it is reproducible: re-running a cell
# produces a different run, not the same log.
#
# The comment that stood here said all of that and then ignored `*.log` anyway,
# so 133 of the 142 files in out/ were untracked while the text above them
# argued they were evidence. That is the prose-vs-code drift this project keeps
# finding in its own harness, sitting in its own .gitignore.
#
# CREDENTIAL CHECK, actually run rather than asserted (2026-09-08):
# scanned out/ and logs/ for sk_/pk_/whsec_, PEM blocks, bearer tokens and
# postgres URLs carrying a password. One hit, excluded below. The launcher
# writes the generated Postgres password into the workspace .env and never
# echoes it. Re-run the scan before adding new log directories - a leaked
# secret in git history is not undone by a later commit.
*.log
!out/**/*.log
!logs/**/*.log
# The one hit: a scrypt salt:hash for the relay's synthetic test user. A hash,
# not a usable credential, and excluded anyway because the standard above is
# only worth anything if it is enforced when it costs something.
out/serve_M_k1.log
# THE RUNS ARE THE RESULTS, so their source is tracked.
#
# This was a blanket `workspace/` ignore, which threw away every artifact any run
# has ever produced in order to avoid node_modules. 120+ run directories, zero
# tracked files - including M_k1's complete Next.js app, the best thing any
# autonomous run has built. Under disk pressure I have been deleting from these
# directories all night with nothing but the filesystem standing between a result
# and its loss.
#
# Source only: 16MB across 1,766 files. What stays ignored is what is
# reproducible from that source, plus anything holding a credential.
workspace/**/node_modules/
workspace/**/.next/
workspace/**/.pnpm-store/
workspace/**/generated/
workspace/**/dist/
# Secrets, never. workspace/M_e1/relay/.env.local holds Stripe test keys, and
# every run's .env carries a generated Postgres password.
workspace/**/.env
workspace/**/.env.*

# Run artifacts are committed, but per-run auth state is not: these are
# localhost session cookies/ids from the relay app the agent builds. Nothing
# in src/ or probe/ reads them, so excluding them costs no analytic evidence.
workspace/**/relay/tmp-state/
workspace/**/*cookies*.txt

# published artifacts: raw run data ships under CC BY 4.0
!data/
!data/*.csv.gz
